Phase 1 review fix (DECISIONS #review-1-r0 F1 — Claude finding 1 blocker, Sol finding 6 required, Grok finding 1; Michael's 1.9 record in #002-outline-feel, escalated by him to a PRD §6 portability defect): a paragraph or heading edited in the rendered view keeps ProseMirror's text verbatim (`leafToMdast`/`pmToMdast`, packages/editor/src/schema.ts), so an ordinary trailing space before Enter reaches `format`, whose `unsafe` rule escapes a space before a line ending as `&#x20;` — `hello ` + Enter + `world` → `hello&#x20;

world
`; `- one ` + Enter → `- one&#x20;
`. `parse` already discards these spaces (micromark strips the leading and trailing whitespace of a paragraph line), so the editor hands the serializer a tree no Markdown file parses to, and the copied Markdown is not a `format(parse(x))` fixed point. Fix in `pmToMdast` (schema.ts), so every consumer of the editor's tree agrees with `parse` — not in the serializer's unsafe table (Grok: do not weaken it) and not at the DevEditor copy button: strip exactly the whitespace micromark strips at the boundary of a paragraph, heading or table cell — leading ASCII whitespace of the block's first text run and trailing whitespace of its last — with the ownership rule stated once in the doc comment. Untouched: a text run adjacent to a `break` node (a hard break already serialises correctly), inline code, code blocks, and the opaque `raw`/`html`/`yaml` bytes; a run that becomes empty is dropped, not kept as an empty text node. Then close the blind spot Claude's risk 1 names: every round-trip leg today is seeded from `parse(fixture)`, so no test can reach a tree only the editor builds. Add one corpus leg seeded from the editor's own output — for every fixture in fixtures/markdown/index.json, build `mdastToPM(parse(x))`, apply a typing-shaped ProseMirror transaction that appends a space to the end of every paragraph and heading, and assert that `format(pmToMdast(doc))` is a fixed point of parse∘format (`format(parse(out)) === out`) and equals `format(parse(x))`; the same leg on the unchanged doc is the absence case. Title the leg `editor fixed point` in the test name. Playwright on /dev/editor: type `X`, space, Enter, `Y` — the markdown pane reads `X

Y
`; the absence case (no space) reads the same; a list item typed with a trailing space serialises without the entity; a heading typed with a trailing space likewise. One test per guard, enumerated from the diff (leading strip, trailing strip, break-adjacent untouched, inline code untouched, raw untouched, empty run dropped, table cell), the journal naming the test that discharges each. Scope: packages/editor/src/schema.ts, packages/editor/test/**, e2e/web/*.spec.ts, docs/lessons.md, the journal. Zero new dependencies (PRD §4).

Phase 1 review fix (DECISIONS #review-1-r5 K2 — Claude finding 2, Sol finding 2 and Grok finding 1, should-fix Required by all three; the `[1.40, found outside scope]` backlog line's trigger fired, its revisit being the r5 reconciliation; `placeChildren` in packages/core/src/positions.ts, the position map of passed task 1.2, whose record is not edited, and the pin task 1.40 left in packages/core/test/positions-corpus.test.ts): a text child whose edge character `containerPhrasing` rewrote after the child's handler returned is not found by `container.indexOf(child.value, cursor)` (positions.ts:455), so it is reported in `unresolved`, `cursorMap` (packages/editor/src/toggle.ts) has no range and no spelling table for it, `nodeAt` over its bytes answers the paragraph, and `toSource` of a caret inside the neighbour falls to `afterLastNode` — the end of the preceding run, inside its closing delimiter. Reproduced by the reconciliation headlessly at 3dd9c4b: `formatWithMap(parse("x *a.*&#x62;
")).map.unresolved` is `["0.2"]`, `~~a.~~&#x62;` gives `["0.1"]`, `&#x62;*.a* x` gives `["0.0"]` (both sides, all three marks; `x *a.* b` is empty); through `cursorMap(pmToMdast(mdastToPM(parse(·))), doc)` on `Alpha ~~beta.~~&#x67;amma delta` every ProseMirror position from 13 (inside `gamma`) to 23 (the end) answers `{ line: 1, ch: 13 }` and `toRendered` of that answers 12, and on `x *a.*&#x62;` the position after `b` (6) answers `{ line: 1, ch: 5 }` — in a browser, toggle then type `X` puts the keystroke inside the marked run (`Alpha ~~beta.X~~gamma delta`, Claude; `x *a.X*b`, Sol). After task 1.45 the rewrite is a whole scalar (`&#x1F600;` for 😀), so the neighbour of an astral character is the same shape with a two-unit character. Do four things. (1) In `placeChildren` (or `wrapHandle`, whichever keeps the lookup in one place — state which in the doc comment): when `indexOf` misses a `text` child, retry the value with its first code point replaced by that code point's numeric character reference (`&#x` + the code point in upper-case hexadecimal, no padding, `;` — the form encode-character-reference.js and 1.45's wrapper write), then with its last code point replaced, then with both — the only rewrites `container-phrasing.js` and the wrapper make, enumerated in the doc comment with the reason —, and a one-character value with the whole value as the reference; the lookup bounded from `cursor` as before, so a later repeated literal is never mistaken for this child (Sol's rule); the found emission's length is the rewritten string's. (2) `spellingOffsets` already reads a reference for a BMP character (`spellingEnd` compares `String.fromCodePoint(code)` with one UTF-16 unit); make it place a surrogate pair written as one reference, with the ownership rule stated once in `SpellingTable`'s doc comment and tested at the first, middle and last position of a text node: the leading unit owns the whole reference and the trailing unit is a zero-width item at the reference's end (its `start` and `end` both the reference's end), so `toSource` of the position between the two units — a position the editor never offers, ProseMirror counting units — answers the reference's end and every other position of the node is monotone; a raw surrogate pair in plain text keeps its two one-unit spellings as today. Rewrite the doc comment's sentence "A character whose spelling is empty cannot arise" to name this one case. (3) Delete `OUTSIDE_ENCODED_NEIGHBOUR` and the `it.fails` case in positions-corpus.test.ts so `strikethrough-punctuation.md` runs through the ordinary "maps every node of the tree, and nothing is unresolved" case (count from the index, never a literal); unit guards in packages/core/test (positions.test.ts or a new file) for `x *a.*&#x62;`, `x **a.**&#x62;`, `~~a.~~&#x62;`, `&#x62;*.a* x`, `~~a.~~&#x1F600;`, `x &#x10400;*(a)*`, `&#x1F600;~~(a.)~~&#x1F600;` (both sides, three marks, one BMP and two astral, a one-character neighbour and a longer one), each asserting `unresolved` empty, the neighbour's range covering the reference, `nodeAt` inside the reference answering the text node, and the spelling table's entries for the encoded character and its neighbours. Asserted able to fail, recorded in the journal and not committed: the retry disabled goes red on the corpus case for `strikethrough-punctuation.md`. (4) In packages/editor/test/position-map-editor-leg.test.ts, a clause in the deletion leg — seeded by `deleteBesideEveryMarkedRun` of typing-legs.ts (imported, unchanged) over every fixture in the index, plus one hand-seeded document `mdastToPM(parse("~~a.~~&#x1F600;
"))` so the astral shape is asserted before 1.47's fixture joins the index — asserting, for every text node the deletion left directly against a flanking mark, that `toSource` is monotone over the node's positions (excluding the position between a pair's units) and that `toRendered(toSource(p))` is `p` for each, with the reach count of such nodes asserted `> 0` and `strikethrough-punctuation.md` named among the fixtures reached; and one Playwright case in a new e2e/web/editor-toggle-encoded-neighbour.spec.ts (helpers copied from editor-strikethrough-neighbour.spec.ts and editor-toggle-trailing-break.spec.ts): load `Alpha ~~beta.~~ gamma delta
`, click the paragraph's end and assert the anchor `{ text: " gamma delta", offset: 12 }`, `ArrowLeft` ×11 asserted at offset 1, one `Backspace` (the 1.41 route; the pane `Alpha ~~beta.~~&#x67;amma delta
`), `ArrowRight` ×3 asserted at `{ text: "gamma delta", offset: 3 }` (the text node's name read from the DOM after the Backspace, not assumed — assert whatever the DOM reports and record it in the journal), `ControlOrMeta+/` (the toggle chord, allowed — the guard bans Home/End chords only), type `X`, toggle back, Copy Markdown → the spy's bytes `Alpha ~~beta.~~&#x67;amXma delta
` with `toBe`, a fixed point, one `delete`, and the rendered paragraph's `textContent` `Alpha beta.gamXma delta`. Caret placement only by a click asserted first and counted horizontal arrows (DECISIONS #022, #024). Scope: packages/core/src/positions.ts, packages/core/test/**, packages/editor/test/position-map-editor-leg.test.ts, e2e/web/editor-toggle-encoded-neighbour.spec.ts, docs/lessons.md, the journal. No change to toggle.ts, typing-legs.ts, format.ts or any fixture, no config or workflow edits, zero new dependencies (PRD §4). Each attempt appends a NEW `- [<id>] ` journal line to docs/progress/journal-main.md, stubbed first by one `printf` that prints the timestamp (`printf -- '- [%s] %s Task: …' <id> "$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"`) and completed in place before the commit that prints DONE — an earlier attempt's line is never edited; completing an earlier attempt's stub and appending nothing is `NO-JOURNAL` even with DONE printed and the suite green (lessons [1.29], [1.41]). Run the suite once: after the implementation is complete, `pnpm lint && pnpm test && cargo test` and the e2e/web suite each one time, then complete the stub, commit and print DONE — the runner re-runs the whole suite on the squashed candidate (RUNNER-SPEC §4), and a second verification pass in the same attempt is what the r5 chain's turn caps were spent on (lessons [1.41], [1.42]). A defect found outside this scope gets a docs/V1.1-BACKLOG.md line with a revisit trigger and a hard stop in this task's commit, never only a lesson or a test comment (DECISIONS #review-1-r1). Procedure note (DECISIONS #review-1-r2 H7): this task's generated `PROMPT.md` wrapper still lists the pre-1.verify.r2 iteration steps (implement, then one journal entry, one commit); CLAUDE.md's stub-first `## Every iteration` list is the one that stands — the wrapper's own line 1 says CLAUDE.md outranks it, the mismatch is mechanical (commit granularity), and it is not a conflict to stop on — so stub the journal, commit, implement, complete the stub.

Windows lib test harness manifest, repair 1 of the 2.verify.g1h GATE-FAILED at a1 (RUNNER-SPEC §2 rewrite rule (a); ci.yml run 36300536766 at 2c5fe44, ref ci/2.verify.g1/a1; evidence /logs/ci/2.verify.g1h/a1/). Every job is green except `test (windows-latest)` → Cargo test: the build finishes, then `Running unittests src\lib.rs (target\debug\deps\desktop_lib-7d351be2f1432d5a.exe)` exits `0xc0000139, STATUS_ENTRYPOINT_NOT_FOUND` before any test runs (workflow.log lines 25969-25973; test-logs/test-logs-windows-latest/cargo-test.log tail). Cause: tauri-build 2.6.3 embeds the Windows application manifest (its src/windows-app-manifest.xml, the Common-Controls 6.0.0.0 dependency) through tauri-winres → embed-resource, which emits `cargo:rustc-link-arg-bins` (embed-resource 3.0.11 src/lib.rs:443), so only bin targets get it; Cargo's `LinkArgTarget::Bin` applies to `target.is_bin()` only, and the lib unit-test harness is a Lib target in test mode (so `rustc-link-arg-tests` would not reach it either). Without the manifest the loader binds comctl32 v5 and cannot resolve `TaskDialogIndirect`, which rfd 0.16 (`common-controls-v6`, forced by tauri-plugin-dialog 2.7.3) and muda 0.19 (tauri's default `common-controls-v6` feature) import by name. The bin proves the contrast: `e2e-shell (windows-latest)` in the same run passed 7/7 with the same imports plus the resource manifest. Fix, the upstream route (tauri-apps discussion #11179): on CARGO_CFG_TARGET_OS == "windows" and CARGO_CFG_TARGET_ENV == "msvc" only, build with `tauri_build::WindowsAttributes::new_without_app_manifest()` (the .rc no longer carries RT_MANIFEST; icon and version info stay) and emit `cargo:rustc-link-arg=/MANIFEST:EMBED` and `cargo:rustc-link-arg=/MANIFESTINPUT:<CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR>/windows-app-manifest.xml` — plain `rustc-link-arg` applies to every linked target of the package, so the bin keeps its manifest and the test harness gains one. Every other target keeps `try_build(Attributes::new())`, which is what `build()` calls today. Replace apps/desktop/src-tauri/build.rs with exactly the following, and add apps/desktop/src-tauri/windows-app-manifest.xml as a byte-for-byte copy of tauri-build 2.6.3's src/windows-app-manifest.xml from the container's cargo registry (copy the file; do not retype it). Zero new dependencies; nothing else changes.

```rust
// build.rs — tauri-build's Windows resource (icon, version info, app manifest) reaches bin targets
// only: tauri-winres -> embed-resource emits `cargo:rustc-link-arg-bins`, and Cargo's
// `LinkArgTarget::Bin` applies to `target.is_bin()`, never to the lib's unit-test harness
// (`desktop_lib-*.exe`). Without the manifest the loader binds comctl32 v5 and the harness dies at
// load with STATUS_ENTRYPOINT_NOT_FOUND (rfd's and muda's `TaskDialogIndirect` are comctl32 v6
// imports; 2.verify.g1h a1, run 36300536766). On windows/msvc the manifest therefore comes from
// the linker for every linked target instead (`/MANIFEST:EMBED` + `/MANIFESTINPUT`, the route
// tauri-apps discussion #11179 gives), and tauri-build is told not to put it in the `.rc` as well,
// which would be a duplicate RT_MANIFEST resource. Other targets are unchanged: `try_build(
// Attributes::new())` is what `tauri_build::build()` calls.
fn main() {
    let target_os = std::env::var("CARGO_CFG_TARGET_OS").unwrap_or_default();
    let target_env = std::env::var("CARGO_CFG_TARGET_ENV").unwrap_or_default();

    let mut attributes = tauri_build::Attributes::new();
    if target_os == "windows" && target_env == "msvc" {
        let manifest = std::path::Path::new(&std::env::var("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR").unwrap())
            .join("windows-app-manifest.xml");
        println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed={}", manifest.display());
        println!("cargo:rustc-link-arg=/MANIFEST:EMBED");
        println!("cargo:rustc-link-arg=/MANIFESTINPUT:{}", manifest.display());
        attributes = attributes
            .windows_attributes(tauri_build::WindowsAttributes::new_without_app_manifest());
    }

    if let Err(error) = tauri_build::try_build(attributes) {
        println!("{error:#}");
        std::process::exit(1);
    }
}
```
